# Solidity unit tests — no mock contracts

**Never** deploy helper / mock / stub Solidity contracts inside `test/unit/**`. All external-contract behaviour must be stubbed with Foundry cheatcodes. This keeps unit tests hermetic, fast, and free from hidden mock-contract bugs.

## Forbidden

- Inline test-only contracts that mimic external dependencies (`MockERC20`, `MockHats`, `SquadAdminImplV2Mock`, `FakeQuartermaster`, etc.).
- Extending production contracts solely to expose internals or override behaviour for tests.
- Using OpenZeppelin / Solmate / similar token-mock helpers from dependencies.

## Required

Stage external behaviour with `vm.mockCall` / `vm.mockCallRevert`. If bytecode must exist at a target address (e.g. a `call` to `.code.length > 0`), use `vm.etch(addr, hex'00')`. Read and assert storage with `vm.load` / `vm.store`. Stage state with `vm.prank`, `vm.warp`, `vm.roll`, `vm.deal`.

```solidity
// BAD — helper mock contract in a test file
contract MockHats {
  mapping(address => mapping(uint256 => bool)) _wearers;
  function isWearerOfHat(address a, uint256 h) external view returns (bool) {
    return _wearers[a][h];
  }
}

// GOOD — mock the external call directly
address constant _HATS = address(uint160(uint256(keccak256('test.HATS'))));
vm.etch(_HATS, hex'00');
vm.mockCall(_HATS, abi.encodeWithSelector(IHats.isWearerOfHat.selector, _user, _hatId), abi.encode(true));
```

## Proxy / delegatecall targets

**EIP-1167 clones** and anything that `delegatecall`s a real implementation need **real bytecode** at the implementation address (the EVM will not let you mock delegatecall targets the way you mock `interface` calls). Deploy **production master copies** — never test-only subclasses — when the test exercises clone init or logic running behind a clone.

Where a fixture still uses an **upgradeable proxy** elsewhere in the codebase, swapping implementation needs a real contract at the new implementation address; you may assert ERC-1967 slots with `vm.load` if applicable.

## Accepted exceptions

- **Production contracts** (including their abstracts) deployed as the contract under test, clone masters, or upgrade targets when upgrades exist.
- **`forge-std/Test.sol`** primitives (`Test`, `Vm`, `StdUtils`, etc.).
- **Integration tests** (`test/integration/**`) — these live outside this rule's scope and may spin up real peer contracts by design.
